engine-strict=true

# `provenance` is deliberately NOT set here.
#
# npm can only generate provenance from a CI provider with OIDC (GitHub Actions), so
# setting it in project config makes every local `pnpm publish` abort with
# `EUSAGE: Automatic provenance generation not supported for provider: null` — breaking the
# only publish path that exists today. It also cannot be waved off at the call site:
# `--provenance=false` is not a `pnpm publish` flag, so pnpm drops it and npm reads this
# file anyway.
#
# It belongs in the release workflow, where OIDC is real: `npm publish --provenance`, or
# `provenance: true` alongside `id-token: write` permissions. T037 owns that.
